1. She experiences significant anxiety when being outside in public. (Verbatim: "Being outside it's really difficult for me I mean I'm sure people have it worse...")
2. She finds crowded environments particularly stressful due to lack of personal space and unpredictable movement. (Verbatim: "Here there's no order to how everybody walks through the city or town or whatever...")
3. She feels more in control of her anxiety when she is with other people, especially when helping someone else who may also be anxious. (Verbatim: "I think when I'm with another person I feel like I have a bit more control within the crowd...")
4. She finds the walking culture in Japan to be more organized and less stressful than in her current location. (Verbatim: "In Japan everyone naturally tries to make streams of like one everyone going one way...")
5. She has been pushed into the road by others while walking, despite trying to be mindful and confident. (Verbatim: "People be coming towards me and so I get to like the edge of the pavement... they just like walk through me and then I just get knocked into the road...")
6. She prioritizes her dog’s safety over her own comfort when navigating crowded spaces. (Verbatim: "I'll always prioritize my dog's safety if that makes sense like if there's not enough room dog gets to stay on the pavement...")
7. She has a dog who accompanies her outside and helps reduce her anxiety. (Verbatim: "I feel when I go out I'm not as anxious when I have my dog like yeah yeah dog definitely helps...")
8. She is an overthinker when outside, constantly analyzing others' movements to avoid being bumped into. (Verbatim: "I'm definitely an overthinker when I'm out so I'm like trying to analyze everybody's path...")
9. She dislikes being the imposter in multiplayer games, finding it emotionally distressing and stressful. (Verbatim: "I don't like being imposter I don't like being the only imposter that's even worse...")
10. She struggles with the emotional weight of lying and deception in games, even when it's part of gameplay. (Verbatim: "I don't like being imposter I don't like being the only imposter that's even worse...") [end of text]



